Apple today released iOS 26.6.1, iPadOS 26.6.1, visionOS 26.6.1, and macOS 26.6.2, with all of the updates containing security fixes.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/iOS-26-6-1-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1058841" /><br/>
Apple also released iOS 18.7.10 and iPadOS 18.7.10 with security fixes.<br/>
<br/>
All of the iOS and iPadOS updates released today deliver security fixes that were first made available in the iOS 27 and iPadOS 27 betas, according to an <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/148282">Apple support document</a>, which provides more specific details. Likewise, macOS 26.6.2 delivers security fixes that were first made available in the macOS Golden Gate 27 beta.<br/>
<br/>
Apple says visionOS 26.6.1 security fix details are coming soon.<br/>
<br/>
